  url = {https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23302640},
  abstract = {Release Notes Breaking Readers reject NaN, Inf and their spellings in every mode with NonFiniteValue. Column 4 is an integer token. Float spellings, signs and out-of-range values are InvalidFixedFlag. Column 5 is an integer token up to 2^64-1 and is never parsed as a float. A type count of 0 is a legal zero-atom frame. Lines 8 and 9 hold only whitespace, and at end of file they may be absent. A per-type count of 0, or a sign or decimal point in a count field, is InvalidCount. JSON con_spec_version 0 or 1, and any unknown major, is UnsupportedVersion. The default writer float format is binary64 round-trip. Fixed decimals remain available when requested. A v3 frame with a missing or invalid units object fails the write with InvalidUnits. A minor 1 frame with velocities and no units.time is InvalidUnits on read and on write. The builder no longer injects time: fs. The written spelling of the eOn and ASE natural time unit is (amu*angstrom^2/eV)^0.5. The writer does not replace that spelling with spaces. default_v3_units_json supplies length, energy, and mass only. It does not supply time: fs. Trailing whitespace after the last complete frame is ignored and does not open a velocity section. section_arity counts value fields. An unknown-section row has that many values, then a flag, and an optional id. A reserved entry that is not 3 for a vector or 1 for a scalar is InvalidVectorLength. Labels compare case-insensitively after collapsing runs of spaces. An unknown section is skipped only for a newer minor that declares section_arity. Otherwise it is UnknownSection. gzip and zstd envelopes yield every member and every frame. set_lattice_vectors keeps lines 3 and 4 consistent with the lattice matrix. ConFrameBuilder stamps con_spec_minor 1 on a v3 frame when the caller does not set it. set_con_spec_minor and rkr_frame_builder_set_con_spec_minor override that value. The writer does not invent or replace the minor. ConFrameBuilder::set_units and rkr_frame_builder_set_units set the units object from C and C++. Download readcon-core 0.17.0 | File | Platform | Checksum |
|--------|----------|----------|
| readcon-core-aarch64-apple-darwin.tar.xz | Apple Silicon macOS | checksum |
| readcon-core-x86_64-apple-darwin.tar.xz | Intel macOS | checksum |
| readcon-core-x86_64-pc-windows-msvc.zip | x64 Windows | checksum |
| readcon-core-aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.xz | ARM64 Linux | checksum |
| readcon-core-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.xz | x64 Linux | checksum |},
  affiliation = {Science Institute and Faculty of Physical Sciences, University of Iceland}
}

